# What does it cost to read a human genome now?
subtitle: "In 2001 reading one human genome cost $95 million. Guess today's price on a log line, then see how it outran even computer chips."
tags: ["biology","data"]
format: quiz
thumb: "band \"Was $95 million. Now?\" note \"2001\""

## What does it cost to read a human genome now?
text: {"font_size":36}
sources:
    - id: owid
      title: Cost of sequencing a full human genome
      authors: Our World in Data, from the National Human Genome Research Institute
      year: 2022
      url: https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/cost-of-sequencing-a-full-human-genome
      finding: about $95.3 million in 2001, $7.1 million in 2007, $70,000 in 2009, $525 in 2022 (current US$, not adjusted for inflation)
    - id: nhgri
      title: 'DNA Sequencing Costs: Data'
      authors: National Human Genome Research Institute
      year: 2022
      finding: cost per human-sized genome, 2001–2022

    icon dna size 210 set twemoji x 150 y 560 icon_look picture of dna hidden true
    scale cost cites ["owid"] x 50 y 330 width 900 unit dollars min 10 max 1000000000 value 525 log true markers [{"value":95300000,"label":"2001: $95M","color":"#b5482e"},{"value":66000,"label":"chip pace","color":"#8a5fa8"},{"value":7150000,"label":"2007: $7M","color":"#3d3833"}] hidden true
    text times "180,000× cheaper" #2f6b8f cites ["owid"] x 600 y 600 font_size 60 hidden true
    text moore "chips: ×2 per 2 years" #8a5fa8 x 600 y 600 font_size 48 hidden true
    text fall_l "÷100 by 2009" #b5482e cites ["owid"] x 600 y 600 font_size 56 hidden true

    card title "What does reading a genome cost now?"

What does it cost to read one person's whole genome, all three billion letters of their DNA?
    draw dna cost

In 2001, when the first genomes were finished, the price was about ninety-five million dollars each.
    draw cost_marker_1

    ask "Click where you think the price was in 2022. Each step is ten times the last." on cost store g default "100000"
        right: Close: you said {g}, and it was about {g.true}.
        wrong: You said {g}. It was about {g.true}: much further down.

About five hundred dollars: a hundred and eighty thousand times cheaper in twenty-one years.
    draw times

    erase times

Compare computer chips, famous for improving fast: their power doubles about every two years.
    draw moore

At that pace, a genome would still cost about sixty-six thousand dollars today.
    draw cost_marker_2

    erase moore

Instead the price fell off a cliff around 2008, when new machines began reading millions of short DNA snippets at once.
    draw cost_marker_3 fall_l

From seven million dollars in 2007 to seventy thousand in 2009: already where the chip pace only gets to today.
    highlight fall_l

    erase fall_l

So a project that once took an international team thirteen years is now an ordinary lab test.
    text lab "13 years → a lab test" #2f6b8f x 600 y 600 font_size 52

